        "original_id": "b2c44d58-1d53-53d6-b437-1a0c75c9cb0a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Don Chafin\n- Places: Logan County, West Virginia; southwestern West Virginia coalfields\n- Events: Battle of Blair Mountain\n- Roles: sheriff; commander\n- Organizations: Logan Defenders\n- Topics: coal miners; strikebreakers; coal mine operators; unionization\n\nFacts:\n- Don Chafin was born on June 26, 1887.\n- In late August and early September 1921, the Battle of Blair Mountain lasted five days in Logan County, West Virginia.\n- During the Battle of Blair Mountain, about 10,000 armed coal miners confronted about 3,000 lawmen and strikebreakers called the Logan Defenders.\n- During the Battle of Blair Mountain, coal mine operators backed the Logan Defenders while the miners attempted to unionize the southwestern West Virginia coalfields.\n- Don Chafin was the sheriff of Logan County, West Virginia, and a commander in the Battle of Blair Mountain.\n- Don Chafin died on August 9, 1954.",
